{
  "card": "Warrior's Blades",
  "title": "the equip discount for +1/+1 counters on the target is dropped, so equip always costs {3}",
  "status": "active",
  "kind": "parser",
  "upstream_issue": null,
  "marks_supported": true,
  "applies_to": {
    "server_version": "0.116.0",
    "build_commit": "3f79456",
    "card_data_sha256": "c4cfb737d0c0b1b135d3a353d71a95606f6ee147727bc11c3d16b82ece33da41",
    "entry_sha256": "2e3434a2a4a18bc23c1c6128cde2e50a00d7966481c1e2795e506e97fd7bb318"
  },
  "rules": {
    "oracle": "When this Equipment enters, it deals 3 damage to any target and you gain 3 life.\nEquipped creature gets +2/+1.\nEquip {3}. This ability costs {1} less to activate for each +1/+1 counter on the creature it targets.",
    "cr": [
      "702.6a",
      "602.2b",
      "601.2c",
      "601.2f",
      "122.1a"
    ],
    "actual": "Equip always costs {3}: the second sentence of the equip line is dropped, so +1/+1 counters on the target give no discount.",
    "expected": "The equip cost is determined after its target is chosen (CR 602.2b, 601.2c, 601.2f): {3} minus {1} for each +1/+1 counter on the creature it targets, never below {0} (generic mana can't be reduced below zero, CR 601.2f). Only +1/+1 counters on that creature count; counters on other creatures, on the creature it is currently attached to, or other kinds of counters don't.",
    "diagnosis": "The equip line is parsed into the Attach ability with cost {3}, but the trailing \"This ability costs {1} less to activate for each +1/+1 counter on the creature it targets.\" is swallowed (the dynamic quantity \"+1/+1 counter on the creature it targets\" isn't recognized), so no cost_reduction is attached. The same sentence with \"each color of the creature it targets\" (Dragonfire Blade) already produces cost_reduction with a Target-scoped count.",
    "suggested_fix": "In the activated-ability self cost-reduction parser (the path that builds AbilityDefinition.cost_reduction for Dragonfire Blade's \"costs {1} less to activate for each color of the creature it targets\"), accept \"for each <counter> counter on the creature it targets\" and emit cost_reduction {amount_per: 1, count: Ref(CountersOn{scope: Target, counter_type: <counter>})}. The runtime already classifies CountersOn{scope: Target} as target-dependent (quantity_ref_reads_target_object) and applies it at committed-target cost settlement.",
    "override_note": "The patch adds cost_reduction {amount_per: 1, count: CountersOn{scope: Target, counter_type: P1P1}} to the equip ability, Dragonfire Blade's shape with the count Oblivion's Hunger uses for +1/+1 counters on a target. The engine treats a Target-scoped count as target-dependent and locks the cost when the target is committed, which is the order CR 602.2b and 601.2c/601.2f require (targets first, then the total cost), and the reduction only reduces generic mana, so it can't go below {0}. The cost is paid when it is determined, so counters added or removed afterward don't change it. Tested on 0.116.0: {3}/{2}/{1}/{0}/{0} for 0/1/2/3/5 counters, the count follows the chosen target, -1/-1 counters don't count, and re-equipping reads the new target. Also checked by hand (not expressible as a test, since upstream can't activate it): with no mana at all, equip onto a creature with three +1/+1 counters is offered and resolves."
  },
